WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.862
Job four: connect your team to the rest of Vanderbilt.

2
00:00:04.912 --> 00:00:13.085
Why it matters: your team needs things it does not control: approvals, information, help from other offices,

3
00:00:13.135 --> 00:00:17.121
and a fair hearing when someone asks too much of you.

4
00:00:17.171 --> 00:00:23.670
Most new managers do not know this is part of the job, so it is the one they do least.

5
00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:29.380
Three habits. Know the people: your HR partner, your Engagement Consultant,

6
00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:36.538
the person in Finance who approves your requests, and a peer manager in another unit, by name,

7
00:00:36.588 --> 00:00:40.650
before you need any of them. Watch for what is coming:

8
00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:48.036
read the compensation calendar in August and tell your team in September what October will bring,

9
00:00:48.086 --> 00:00:50.472
instead of hearing it from them.

10
00:00:50.522 --> 00:00:57.554
Speak up for your team: when another office’s request would break your month, show the hours,

11
00:00:57.604 --> 00:01:05.245
name the conflict, offer two options, and negotiate the date, instead of absorbing it or refusing it.

12
00:01:05.295 --> 00:01:10.118
What to stop doing: meeting your HR partner at the first crisis.

13
00:01:10.168 --> 00:01:14.686
This week: have coffee with one person your team depends on.

14
00:01:14.736 --> 00:01:20.397
Now flip the three cards on the page; your call on that request comes next.

